# Ignore rules for the Fit project root.
#
# Two of these are not housekeeping — they are the reason this file exists at all.

# THE THROWAWAY PLATFORM SPIKE. Its own git repository on a public branch, kept only for the
# findings it produced. Its code is discarded and must never become part of the application.
/spike/

# PRESERVED SPIKE EVIDENCE. Deliberately untracked and MUST NEVER BE COMMITTED ANYWHERE: it
# quotes the coach's real Drive identifiers, calendar identifiers and signed-in account. The
# repository is public by a knowing decision, so anything here reaching it is a real leak, and one
# that no credential scanner would catch because none of it is shaped like a credential.
/_spike-evidence/

# Dependencies. Restored with `npm install`, never committed.
node_modules/

# Local environment and editor noise.
.env
.env.*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log

# NOT IGNORED, DELIBERATELY: app/dist/.
# The published site is a static host with no build step of its own, so the built output is
# committed on purpose. Adding it here would publish an empty site. Run `npm run check:stale`
# before publishing to confirm it matches its source.
